#
# Lines are "key value". Keys:
#   have NAME [VALUE]  the environment provides NAME, satisfying "needs NAME";
#                      a VALUE reaches the tests as PC_HAVE_<NAME>
#
# Names in use:
#   have kill_uid U    a user ID no process uses, for XSH.kill.005: it sends
#                      kill(-1, SIGURG) as that user, which reaches every
#                      process of that user on the machine
#
# Planned names (tests do not use them yet):
#   have faultdev   a scratch disk that fails chosen sectors on command
#   have lowmem     a VM booted with little memory and no swap
#   have uid2       a second unprivileged user, named by "user2"
#
# have faultdev
# have kill_uid 2000000123
